===Climate===
[[File:Miyagi Tropical Beach.jpg|thumb|left|250px|A popular beach resort near Amami during the dry winter season.]]

Miyagi Prefecture experiences temperatures above 20 °C (68 °F) for the majority of the year. Due to its unique geographical span along the northern maritime frontier, the climate ranges from a humid subtropical climate (Köppen climate classification Cfa) in the southern districts closer to the central mainland, to a tropical rainforest climate (Köppen climate classification Af) in the extreme northern coastal cities near the Yanbaru border.

Because of this constant equatorial warmth, snowfall is practically unheard of at sea level anywhere in the prefecture. However, a highly unusual meteorological anomaly occurred on January 24, 2016, when sleet was recorded in the northern coastal city of Akune for the first time in modern history.

As illustrated by the climate data for the capital city of Shinagawa below, the region is defined by extreme seasonal precipitation shifts rather than temperature fluctuations. The data highlights a massive spike in rainfall during June and July, frequently exceeding 500 millimeters in a single month. This torrential period corresponds with the arrival of the Eastern Typhoons sweeping in from the Shendan Ocean. Following the wet season, temperatures peak in August with highs routinely surpassing 32 °C (90 °F) combined with oppressive humidity. Conversely, the winter months from November through February are remarkably mild and relatively dry, making the prefecture a popular year-round coastal destination.

